==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
1538 as noun, 1660 as verb. By reduplication. Perhaps from a dialectal word or Scandinavian; compare Old Norse {{m|non|flim||[[lampoon]], [[mockery]]}}.<ref>{{R:Online Etymology Dictionary}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|æm|lang=en}}
* {{IPA|/ˈflɪmflæm/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[flim]]-[[flam]]}} (Not recorded with this spelling in major dictionaries; usually spelled [[flimflam]].)

# Misinformation; [[bunkum]]; false information presented as true.
#: ''Most reports of supernatural occurrences turn out to be '''flim-flam''' when carefully investigated.''
# [[confidence game]], [[con game]]
# {{lb|en|archaic}} [[table tennis]]

